# Product-molecularity fixture: 20 ten-member rings L.R.L.R.L.R.L.R.L.R and the
# single rule L(r!1).R(l!1) -> L(r) + R(l). Breaking one bond leaves L and R
# connected the long way round (eight more molecules), so the products never
# separate: BNG2.pl generates no reaction and Lfree, the count of L with a free
# site, stays 0. The search that tests this must go past its first budget.
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  L(r,r)
  R(l,l)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  L(r!1,r!2).R(l!2,l!3).L(r!3,r!4).R(l!4,l!5).L(r!5,r!6).R(l!6,l!7).L(r!7,r!8).R(l!8,l!9).L(r!9,r!10).R(l!10,l!1) 20
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Lfree L(r)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  L(r!1).R(l!1) -> L(r) + R(l) k
end reaction rules
end model
writeXML()
